1
00:00:00,150 --> 00:00:02,728
This animal has three hearts.

2
00:00:03,008 --> 00:00:05,637
And its blood is blue.

3
00:00:06,087 --> 00:00:08,612
Two hearts push blood through the gills.

4
00:00:08,892 --> 00:00:11,249
The third sends it to the rest of the body.

5
00:00:11,529 --> 00:00:15,755
And when the octopus swims, that third heart stops beating.

6
00:00:16,205 --> 00:00:20,826
Its blood is blue because it carries oxygen with copper,

7
00:00:21,106 --> 00:00:23,057
not with iron like ours.

8
00:00:23,507 --> 00:00:25,563
Its arms think, too.

9
00:00:25,843 --> 00:00:29,894
About two thirds of its neurons are in its arms,

10
00:00:30,174 --> 00:00:32,912
working more than two thousand suckers.

11
00:00:33,362 --> 00:00:38,745
It can change its colour, pattern and even skin texture in a flash,

12
00:00:39,025 --> 00:00:42,606
even though its eyes have only one kind of colour receptor.

13
00:00:43,056 --> 00:00:46,899
And with all of this, it lives only one to two years.

14
00:00:47,179 --> 00:00:50,006
Imagine what it could learn with more time.
